%% Data Flow - Asynchronous Create via SQS

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client
    participant ALB as Application Load Balancer
    participant ECS as ECS Fargate Task
    participant SQS as SQS Queue<br/>(create-queue)
    participant Consumer as Lambda SQS Consumer<br/>(Private Subnet)
    participant RDS as RDS MySQL
    participant DLQ as Dead Letter Queue

    Note over Client,DLQ: Async CREATE Flow

    Client->>+ALB: POST /queue<br/>{"table": "items", "data": {...}}
    ALB->>+ECS: Forward request
    ECS->>ECS: Build SQS message
    ECS->>+SQS: SendMessage<br/>(via NAT Gateway → AWS API)
    SQS-->>-ECS: MessageId: "abc-123"
    ECS-->>-ALB: 202 {"messageId": "abc-123"}
    ALB-->>-Client: HTTP 202 Accepted

    Note over SQS,RDS: Background Processing

    SQS->>+Consumer: Trigger (batch of messages)
    Consumer->>Consumer: Parse message body
    Consumer->>+RDS: INSERT INTO items (...)

    alt Success
        RDS-->>-Consumer: inserted_id
        Consumer->>SQS: Delete message from queue
        Consumer-->>-SQS: Success
    else Failure (up to 3 retries)
        Consumer-->>SQS: Throw error (message visible again)
        SQS->>Consumer: Retry delivery
    else Max Retries Exceeded
        SQS->>DLQ: Move to Dead Letter Queue
        Note over DLQ: Manual investigation required
    end
